// TEST: Diag Equiv Engine Lie Near Miss (diag)
// ERROR: BL4008 @ 18:3
// ERROR-CONTAINS: *sqrt(3)
// ERROR-CONTAINS: The residual's nonzero radical components
// ERROR-CONTAINS: NEAR MISS: the residual is 5.992e-08
// ERROR-CONTAINS: a float literal is its exact dyadic value, so 0.3 is not 3/10
// ERROR-CONTAINS: write the division (3.0 / 10.0 IS 3/10)
// ERROR-CONTAINS: the synthesized basis (ml.derive_linear / ml.derive_tp / ml.derive_poly)
import ml as ml
// 0.5773502 written where 1/sqrt(3) was meant. The l = 1 x l = 1 -> l = 2
// quadratic has an IRRATIONAL coefficient ratio in the shipped real basis, so
// no exact spelling exists and the refusal is permanent — which is exactly the
// case the near-miss note hands to the synthesized (Schur-certified) basis.
// The residual itself is a RADICAL VECTOR: a rational part and a sqrt(3) part,
// rendered componentwise, because componentwise zero is the acceptance test.
let static V = [(1, 1, 1)]
let static Q = [(2, 0, 1)]
function quad(x: Array<Float like IrrepsIdx<V>>) where ml.equiv(O3) -> Array<Float like IrrepsIdx<Q>> =
  [x(0) * x(2),
   x(0) * x(1),
   0.5773502 * (x(1) * x(1) - 0.5 * x(0) * x(0) - 0.5 * x(2) * x(2)),
   x(1) * x(2),
   0.5 * (x(2) * x(2) - x(0) * x(0))]
